      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In two patient groups undergoing coronary surgery (n = 10) hemodynamic side effects of mexiletine and lidocaine were investigated. Changes of clinical importance were seen in cardiac-output, stroke volume, total peripheral resistance, triple- and cardiac index. There are significant differences 10, 15, and 30 min after application (p less than 0.05; p less than 0.025) in cardiac-index."},
